      "math_academy_id": "q-5472",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $P(A)=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Find $P(B|A).$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the definition of the conditional probability $P(B|A):$\n\n$$\nP(B|A)=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(B|A) & =\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
